Z||000000||Shianne||05-16-2001||07:52 PM||||Are the ball joint replaceable or do you have to get a lower arm, I have heard confilicting views.  I have one that is lose and it seems like all it needs is tighting, but I have never yet found a good way to do this.  Any one have a good way to remove and replace or tighted ball joints.<P>Thanks Pat||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||05-16-2001||08:01 PM||||you can replace just the ball joint, rather than the whole control arm.  If it is still the original BJ it will be tack welded in-these welds will have to ground away before pressing the old out, then press new in. so you will need a BJ press.  Are you from south western Ont-if so see thread re meet in Grand Bend june 9th||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shianne||05-16-2001||09:04 PM||||No I am in Alberta.  And I don't think that it is the orginal.  How is the greese nipple, this one is on a 45.  Seems a little different.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Bob Englert||05-16-2001||10:18 PM||||Ball joints are replaceable.  Lower ball joints at AutoZone here are about $16 each!  I had a local machine shop press out the old and press in the new ones after I removed the lower control arms.  This would be a great time to replace the control arm bushings as well.  Get it all done at once.  You will be surprised at the difference.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shianne||05-16-2001||11:12 PM||||Should I put poly bushings back in or just rubber.  I intend to auto solom this car so I am leaning towards a stiffer set up.  Is there a problem with doing this on just one side and the the other shortly there after.  Is there a diffrent grade of ball joints or are they all standard.<P>Where is the best place to by the poly bushing in canada or am I better off to get them in the states.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||N_Man||05-17-2001||01:15 AM||||Shianne, what part of alberta are you from?<P>Get MOOG ball joints, they are high quality and have a good warranty.<P>Poly is availiable from performance shops but is somtimes cheaper to order.<P>I wouldnt do one side without doing the other.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shianne||05-17-2001||09:49 AM||||I am from Pincher Creek, the far south west corner.  I do make it in to Calgary quite often.  I have also Been on the Calgary Fiero owners group page.  Is there some one local that has those bushings in Calgary? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||N_Man||05-17-2001||08:31 PM||||If you want to get them in town you WILL have to order them, it will usually take as long as ordering them from the states.<P>Try calling unlimited performance and exaust OR mopac<BR>Mopac is usually the best deal but can be a pain to deal with when you say the parts are for a fiero.||||reg||1
